meta {
  name: Sim route for an unsaved shape
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/courses/sim-route
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "roundingM": 15,
    "startLine": { "ax": -40, "ay": 0, "bx": 40, "by": 0 },
    "finishLine": { "sameAs": "start" },
    "marks": [
      { "x": 0, "y": 500, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" },
      { "x": 0, "y": 0, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" },
      { "x": 0, "y": 500, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  200 { roundingM, key, wps:[{x,y,kind,side?,ref?}], passes:[{label,index,kind,required,passed,ok,dist,passDist,range,scored,point,centre}] }
  400 { error }

  Compiles the scripted route for a shape the editor is still working on,
  so the course builder can draw exactly what the simulator will sail
  (todo 32). Nothing is stored: same compiler as GET /courses/:id/sim-route
  and as the run generator.

  Validation is the course validation (a startLine and a finishLine are
  required, 1..10 marks, radius 5..200m) — a lineless course has no route.

  `passes` is the read-out the editor shows: per mark the side it is
  actually left on (`passed` vs `required`), the pass distance, the closest
  approach anywhere on the route (`dist`, which is smaller when the boat
  also sails over that buoy somewhere else), and `range` — how far the buoy
  rotates around the boat while it rounds it. `scored` is `range >= 150°`,
  the number the device uses to call a rounding done; a mark the boat turns
  back around reads ~90° and is never scored.
}
